    <!-- ============================================================================
         Mozart's icon set - Material Symbols (Outlined, weight 400, grade 0, fill 0),
         sourced from fonts.google.com/icons. Single home for every icon used across
         the app: toolbar/window controls, the page context menu, the hamburger menu,
         and the Extensions popup - replaces the old SVGRepo stroke-outline icons and
         the now-removed Themes/ContextMenuIcons.xaml (merged in here).

         Two resource shapes are used, matching how each icon is actually consumed:

         - Geometry  - for icons drawn as a Path directly inline in XAML (toolbar,
           window controls) or built directly in C# (the hamburger menu's Zoom row,
           which is a hand-built StackPanel, not MenuItem.Icon). Used as
           Data="{StaticResource Icon.X}" or (Geometry)FindResource("Icon.X").

         - DataTemplate - for icons shown via MenuItem.Icon (the page context menu,
           the rest of the hamburger menu, and the Extensions popup), which all
           render icons through a fresh ContentControl per item - see
           ContextMenuBuilder.RenderEntry and MainWindow.MenuItem() for the two
           places that look these up via Application.Current.TryFindResource(...).

         Material Symbols icons are solid filled shapes (not stroke skeletons like
         the old icon set), so every Path below is Fill-based (Fill=TextPrimaryBrush,
         no Stroke) - see NavIconPathFilled in App.xaml for the toolbar's matching
         Style. The old NavIconPath/SidebarIconPath styles (Stroke-based) are left
         untouched since Settings/Password Manager/Private windows still use them
         with the old icon set - out of scope for this pass.
    ============================================================================ -->

